WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.137
This query applies several product rules in priority order.

00:00:03.137 --> 00:00:06.242
It checks for a missing product name, missing price, invalid price, and negative stock.

00:00:06.242 --> 00:00:10.997
If none of those selected rules fail, the row passes the selected checks.

00:00:10.997 --> 00:00:16.332
A production system might store several issue codes instead of only the first one,

00:00:16.332 --> 00:00:17.967
but this CASE expression is a clear beginner-friendly start.

00:00:17.967 --> 00:00:21.642
Validation is rule-based detection, not automatic correction.

00:00:21.642 --> 00:00:25.857
A failed email-shape check tells you that a record deserves attention; it does not tell you the correct email.

00:00:25.857 --> 00:00:31.658
Treat quality flags as evidence that can drive quarantine, review, or a documented repair process.
